  faqs: [
    { q: 'Can I book cleaning without sealing?', a: 'Yes. Cleaning only is one of our service options. The assessment helps determine whether the joints also need attention and whether sealing suits the surface. A full clean-and-seal package is not automatically necessary.' },
    { q: 'Will cleaning fix loose pavers or standing water?', a: 'No. Cleaning removes surface buildup; re-sanding replenishes joints. Neither corrects a failed base or drainage slope. Point out movement, sunken areas and puddles during the visit so repairs can be identified before maintenance is planned.' },
    { q: 'What if my pavers already have sealer?', a: 'Tell us when they were last sealed and the product name if you know it. A previous coating, whitening or peeling can change the preparation required. Do not assume a new product can simply be applied over the old one; compatibility and any removal work need assessment.' },
    { q: 'How often should pavers be cleaned and sealed?', a: 'Check the surface and joints periodically rather than automatically adding sealer on a fixed schedule. Cleaning needs and resealing intervals depend on traffic, exposure, condition and the product instructions. We assess whether cleaning, joint maintenance or another coat is appropriate.' },
    { q: 'What if it rains, and when can I use the area again?', a: 'If rain interrupts our work, we come back and finish at no additional charge. The surface still needs the drying and curing conditions required by the selected products. Ask for the specific pedestrian, vehicle and pool-area reopening instructions for your job.' },
    { q: 'What should I prepare for a cleaning and sealing estimate?', a: 'Tell us your city, whether the area is a driveway, patio or pool deck, and what concerns you. Mention previous sealing, stains, loose pavers and puddles. Cost depends on the area, condition, preparation and selected service level; the on-site assessment and itemized written estimate are free.' },
    { q: 'Do you serve Palm Beach Gardens?', a: 'Yes. We offer residential paver cleaning and sealing in Palm Beach Gardens and other Palm Beach County communities, including Boca Raton, Boynton Beach, Delray Beach, Jupiter, Wellington and West Palm Beach. Use the contact form to request an assessment at your property.' },
